    <!-- ROLL-STIFFNESS FIX (kp override, hip_roll/ankle_roll only): two
         earlier attempts at fixing "feet stub together while walking" used
         gravcomp (see git history) -- both improved the inner-edge sole
         gap but destabilized the sagittal balance (one fell during the
         gait itself, the other during the post-walk settle), so gravcomp
         was abandoned entirely, per request, in favor of this simpler
         lever: just raise kp on the two roll joints per leg. A blanket
         kp doubling across EVERY body_servo joint was tried earlier and
         made the gap worse (0.056cm) -- this instead overrides kp on ONLY
         r/l_hip_roll and r/l_ankle_roll, leaving hip_pitch/knee/ankle_pitch
         and everything else at the class default (kp=12).

         Swept kp on just these 4 actuators (gravcomp off, dampratio/
         forcerange left at the class default 0.6 / +-1.667 N*m) through
         the full stand -> go_forward_start -> go_forward x4 ->
         go_forward_end -> 8s-hold trace used to catch the earlier
         regressions: gap rose monotonically with kp and never once
         destabilized (max transient pitch ~18 deg throughout, same as
         baseline's normal gait sway) or saturated the torque cap:
           kp=12 (orig): 0.39cm   kp=24: 0.73cm   kp=48: 0.93cm
           kp=18: 0.60cm          kp=36: 0.85cm   kp=64: 0.99cm
           kp=96: 1.09cm  kp=128: 1.07cm (gains flatten out past ~64-96)
         Picked kp=64 -- past the knee of the curve, comfortably short of
         the point where returns flatten, 0 actuator saturation and 0
         large-tilt events at every kp tested up to 128. -->
    <position name="r_hip_roll" joint="r_hip_roll" class="body_servo" kp="64" ctrlrange="-1.0123 2.1817"/>  <!-- servo 5 -->
